
# Dolt database files (added by bd init)
.dolt/
*.db

# Private specs (not for public release)
docs/specs/01-*.md
docs/specs/02-*.md
docs/specs/03-*.md

# Beads / Dolt files (added by bd init)
# The beads tracker (issues.jsonl, Dolt creds, hooks) is local-only: it carried
# PII (owner emails), homelab topology, and a credential key. Canonical state
# lives in Dolt; do not ship the tracker to public remotes.
.beads/
.beads-credential-key

# Root-built connector/importer binaries (anchored to repo root so they do NOT
# shadow connectors/hackernews, connectors/trello, and importers/mbox -- bare
# entries would match those path components and hide files added under them).
/hackernews
/trello
/mbox

# Binaries from the README's "Building from source" loop, which now builds
# every component (28 of them) rather than a hand-listed ten. Anchored to the
# repo root for the same reason as the entries above.
/glovebox
/*-connector
/*-importer
/rules-sign

# Ruleset signing keys (docs/rule-signing.md). The PRIVATE half must never
# reach this repository: whoever holds it can sign a ruleset that disables
# every boundary in the product, and the whole design rests on it living
# outside the cluster and outside CI. `rules-sign keygen` writes 0600 files
# named like these by default; the patterns are a backstop for the moment
# somebody runs it in a checkout by mistake, not a substitute for keeping
# the key somewhere else entirely.
*.key.pem
ruleset-signing*
!ruleset-signing*.pub
